  "body": "Hi! I'm new here and just came from the tweet I saw mentioning this spec.\n\nWorking every day with unit tests projects, as QUnit, I wonder if we could improve the API for `console.assert`.\n\nI haven't elaborated anything yet, but I've got some immediate ideas that could be very useful for other tests and assertion libraries:\n- register (or maybe store in a buffer) the `console.assert` calls/results\n- record stack trace for each call (Firefox/Chroes does it, Edge doesn't)\n- log/print the assert calls whenever they pass or fail (maybe use \"info\" as the logLevel when it pass).\n- A new observable \"assert\" log level would be interesting to handle every assert log\n\nThese changes can be very helpful for unit test tools and respective cross compatible reporters, e.g. https://github.com/js-reporters/js-reporters.\n",
